    "bitcoin_integration": "Bitcoin is legal and unregulated as a currency in Portugal. Portugal was historically one of the most crypto-friendly jurisdictions in the EU (tax-free crypto until 2023). Since 1 January 2023 (State Budget Law 24-D/2022) a crypto-asset tax regime applies: capital gains on crypto held for less than 365 days are taxed as Category G gains at a flat 28% (or included in aggregated income), while gains on crypto held for 365 days or more are excluded from tax for most residents. The Portuguese Tax Authority (Autoridade Tributária) issued official guidance and binding rulings (e.g. Processo 29052) confirming this."
